{
  "dom_id": "step-q127812",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Determine the interval on which the function $f(t)=\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2t+4),\\,\\frac{2}{t},\\,(t-1)^{3}\u27e9$ is continuous.",
  "worked_solution": "A vector-valued function is continuous on an interval if and only if each of its components is continuous on that interval.\n\nLet's now consider the components of $f(t)$ one by one.\n\n- The function $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2t+4)$ is continuous for $t>-2.$\n\n- The function $\\frac{2}{t}$ is continuous everywhere except the excluded point $t=0.$\n\n- The function $(t-1)^{3}$ is continuous for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is continuous for all $t>-2$ except the point $t=0.$ So the interval of continuity is $(-2,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ).$",
